{"Title":"An Act relative to the safe operation of motor vehicles","BillNumber":"H3451","DocketNumber":"HD3302","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"WMS1","Name":"William M. Straus","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WMS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T11:39:22.963"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"WMS1","Name":"William M. Straus","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WMS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T11:39:22.9633333"},{"Id":"ACM1","Name":"Adrian C. Madaro","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/ACM1","ResponseDate":"2023-07-26T13:42:34.5433333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3451/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Straus of Mattapoisett, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3451) of William M. Straus relative to further regulating distracted driving.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Subsection (a) of section 13B of chapter 90 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the third sentence the following:-\r\n\tNo operator of a motor vehicle shall record, broadcast or otherwise capture images or video of themselves. \r\n\tSECTION 2. Said section 13B of said chapter 90, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by inserting after subsection (a) the following subsection:- \r\n\t(a1/2) An operator shall not view video, images or text unrelated to the operation, maintenance, or navigation of the motor vehicle that is displayed on a monitor, screen or other display installed in the motor vehicle. This subsection shall not apply to: (i) symbols or text that enable or disable the hands-free mode of either a mobile electronic device or an on-board application; (ii) symbols or text related to the use of audio systems; (iii) symbols or text related to the use of equipment installed in the motor vehicle by the manufacturer; (iv) symbols or text related to the use of a dispatch system; (v) video or images of vehicle occupants other than the operator; or (vi) video, images, symbols or text related to the use of traffic engineering equipment.  \r\n\tSECTION 3. Subsection (c) of said section 13B of said chapter 90, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking the words “using a mobile electronic device.”  \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":"Whereas, The deferred operation of this act would tend to defeat its purpose, which is to further regulate distracted driving, therefore it is hereby declared to be an emergency law, necessary for the immediate preservation of the public safety.\r\n\r\n","RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}